---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
const lang = 'en';
---
<Layout
  title="Preparing for your first motorcycle rally-raid in Morocco · CDM Motorsport"
  description="Getting ready for a motorcycle rally-raid in Morocco: experience, fitness, gear, navigation. What you really need to know before your first off-road motorcycle tour."
  ogImage="/img/gallery/gallery-05.jpg"
  lang={lang}
>
  <section class="phero short" style="background-image:url('/img/gallery/gallery-05.jpg')">
    <div class="wrap c">
      <div class="eyebrow" style="color:#e8c9a6">Advice</div>
      <h1>First <em>raid</em></h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pad">
    <div class="wrap article">
      <div class="meta reveal">Advice · 6 min read</div>
      <div class="big reveal" style="margin-bottom:24px">
        Preparing for your first<br />motorcycle raid in <em>Morocco</em>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal">
        <p>
          The question I always get before someone's first trip is: "Is this really for me?"
          Most of the time, the answer is yes. If you already ride off-road, motocross or
          enduro, even just on weekends, you've got the foundation to come along. The rest
          you learn on the trail.
        </p>
        <p>
          What really matters is the drive and a bit of off-road experience. A motivated
          beginner fits right in with a small guided group: we move together, at a pace
          that gives everyone the time to find their rhythm and build confidence.
          <a href="/en/#raids">Discover my raids</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          On the fitness side, you don't need to train like a pro rider. But stacking long
          days in the saddle is more tiring than people imagine, especially in the heat. A
          few weeks of cardio before you come, and you'll enjoy the later stages a whole
          lot more.
          <a href="/en/actualites/preparation-physique-raid">My page on physical preparation</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          For gear, you bring your own protection (helmet, goggles, back protector, elbow
          and knee pads, boots, gloves) and something to protect you from the sun. The
          motorcycle, I provide ready to ride: a KOVE 450 Rally dialed in for the terrain.
          <a href="https://kove-racing.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">KOVE Racing</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          The real learning curve is reading the terrain and navigating. And that's my job:
          I'm here to pass on the right instincts, stage after stage. You just ride,
          observe, and enjoy yourself.
        </p>

        <p style="margin-top:28px">
          Ready to give your first adventure a try?
        </p>
        <a href="/en/reserver" class="btn dark" style="margin-top:14px">Ask me about a date</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
